description:
Visualization of implants and bone model will aid in implant planning in Web Planner. Figma concepts based on formative studies will drive the final arrangement of information. On a higher level following things needs to be considered - 

# 3D bone model - reconstructed 3D bone model from VOLT ( examples - both pelvis (x2), and femur (x2), Femur canal (operative side), Condyles (x2))
# 3D Implant model - Imported from IDB. Mostly solid, different color for each type of component for easy differentiations
# 3D model view options - Ability to zoom, pan, rotate 360 degrees. Some pre-defined views such as Anterior/posterior, medial/lateral, superior inferior. 
# 3D model Opacity/Transparency - Default transparency for each components and ability to change transparency in the range of complete opaque to complete transparent.
# 2D representation of 3D models (used for Implant placement) - Showing the cross-section/outline of 3D models in a specific frame across the depth of 3D models in respective reference plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse). Model can be scrolled to pre-defined slice thickness to view a specific slice. Any landmarks, for example COR are projected through out the slides.
# 2D model view options - Allow user to zoom, pan.
# 2D Xray view - Option to show Xray or DRR if provided by Visionaire Engineer’s plan only for visualization, no processing.
# Ability to expand/shrink screen sizes during implant planning.



