Save force values associated with gap calculations in Pre-Op and Post-Op gap assessment screens. Need to explore whether this should replace the force setting value that is being saved currently or add to current data logs.

*Need for collecting this data*: The Tensioner device is a new product out in the field and it has 3 force thresholds for recommended use in the field. The idea behind collecting this data is to understand how the joint space behaves outside of these force regions since the regions come out of calculations from usability etc and not entirely from the clinical understanding of joint laxity 

*What is to be collected*: Collect all force values that are associated with each transform when the trackers are visible. Create a threshold from when to start collecting this force to avoid collecting dead band force ( Focus on this if space the file is occupying on the disc is a concern) . Additionally add time stamps to collate the data

*What is currently collected*: 1.7 software already captures all gap collections in sequential order (this includes rejected gaps and accepted gaps). The force bucket associated with every bin of gap data is saved in the gap files (rejected and accepted) for every collection.

*Other considerations*: 

* Find creative ways to reduce the data collected. Options:
** Compare transforms and data and save to disk only if they are different
** Decide on a minimum force threshold to begin collecting data
** Add a file size limit
* Save to disk only during state transition to not impact the performance of the state by constantly writing to file
* Run latency test before and after the feature is implemented to ensure the performance has not been affected
* Store ALL planning data as well to recreate the scenarios in post processing. Save planning data along with state transition so that if plan changes , the gap state will reflect the new plan
* Data should be compressed to avoid blowing up the size of a case on CORI
* Compress data at the end of a session. If case is resumed , create a new compression at the end of that session
* *Post processing of collected data is NOT included in this story.* Post processing data should consider the insertion of the Tensioner into the joint space affecting the gaps. This will not be related to application of force since the insertion will happen first before the handle is squeezed. Analyze and identify data pattern to recognize Tensioner insertion
* Save current implant plan (implant selected, position, thickness etc.)



